Go uses (go centric way: Feature Based) project structure

```
my-go-app/
├── cmd/
│   └── server/
│       └── main.go             # Main entry point to boot the app
├── internal/                   # Code hidden from external applications
│   ├── auth/                   # Authentication Domain
│   │   ├── handler.go          # (Controller) Handles HTTP requests
│   │   ├── model.go            # (Model) Database schemas for Auth
│   │   └── repository.go       # Handles direct DB queries
│   ├── users/                  # User Management Domain
│   │   ├── handler.go          # (Controller)
│   │   ├── model.go            # (Model)
│   │   └── service.go          # Core business logic
│   └── database/
│       └── db.go               # Establishes connection pooling
├── pkg/                        # Open source / reusable code (optional)
└── go.mod 
```